.TH MKFS.INVFS 8 "2026-10" "InvariantFS" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
mkfs.invfs \- make an InvariantFS volume (mkfs(8) front-end)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mkfs.invfs
.RB [ \-V ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-q ]
.I device
.RI [ size_gb ]
.br
.B mkfs.invfs
.RB [ \-V ]
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-q ]
.I dev0 size0_gb dev1 size1_gb
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mkfs.invfs
is the standard
.BR mkfs (8)
entry point for fstype
.BR invfs .
It forwards to
.BR invf-mkfs :
one device (or image) plus an optional size in gigabytes, or the
two-device dev0/dev1 form with a size per device.
.PP
Label and UUID options
.RB ( \-L ,
.BR \-U )
are refused, not ignored: format v0 carries a generated volume UUID
but no label field, and silently dropping a
.B \-L
would be a lie the fstab
.B LABEL=
lookup then pays for.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR invf-mkfs (8),
.BR mkfs (8),
.BR invarifs (7)
